  "body": "SerialPort should have the isOpen() method indicating if the port is open or not.\r\n\r\nI have an issue with Chrome (85.0.4183.83) on Mac where this method would be useful.\r\nThere is a known problem on Mac that serial ports are listed twice. When I select one of them and call getPorts() I also get the selected port twice. From reported getInfo() object there is no difference between the both (the name is missing in the info). However only one can be used for communication. Calling open() on the second one always throws an error: \"NetworkError: Failed to open serial port.\"\r\nCalling open() again on the same SerialPort object leads to the next error: \"Failed to execute 'open' on 'SerialPort': The port is already open.\"\r\nSo I realized that there is actually no way to check if a port is already open or not.\r\n\r\nP.S. I can see the described behaviour with the second \"broken\" port also in Chrome on Windows 10. Chrome reports only one port, but always fails on open() showing the same errors: \"NetworkError: Failed to open serial port.\" and \"Failed to execute 'open' on 'SerialPort': The port is already open.\"\r\n\r\nP.P.S. Working with WebUSB I really used to chrome://usb-internals/ and chrome://device-log/. It would be nice if there would be something similar for Web Serial for debugging issues with the serial ports.",
